  "_readme": {
    "purpose": "Product Studio export shaped for the VeriDex rating engine. Verified end to end: importing this creates the LOB binding, coverage tree, product, rating factors with real tables, and eligibility rules — and once the factors are approved on Rating Factors, they fold into a real Commercial Trucking premium.",
    "whyFamilyMatters": "product.family MUST be one of the platform's known lines or the importer creates a brand-new line with no calculator behind it. 'Transportation' / 'Commercial Auto' do NOT match — 'Commercial Trucking' does.",
    "whyGroupNamesMatter": "Each rating group's name becomes the imported factor's `coverage`. Naming a group after a real coverage ('Auto Liability') is what lets the engine fold that factor into that coverage's premium. A group called 'RISK FACTORS' imports fine but never reaches a premium.",
    "amountVsTable": "`amount` becomes the factor's Default Value and is what actually rates (via the RemainingFactors catch-all). `table.data` imports alongside it as this tenant's own browsable rate table. Both are carried here deliberately.",
    "afterUpload": "Factors land as Not wired and awaiting approval by design. Approve each on Rating Factors (a second user must approve — the creator cannot approve their own), then quote the product in Sandbox Quote Generation."
  },
